# Menu drawer contrast allowlist

When contrast checks, DevTools, or a11y tests flag the banner **menu drawer**:

- **Do not** paint selected/current tray text with `--tpl-color-interactive-hover` (pink day / teal night). That pair fails WCAG AA on the purple/lime tray.
- Selected/current tray text uses `--template-menu-drawer-current-text-color` (`#ffe8f8` day / `#062e2b` night).
- Day rest ink is **white** on purple; night rest ink is **black** on lime (nav and user name). Resting underlines are the inverse. Hover is black day / white night.
- The action-row separator may stay **interactive accent at 0.62** (non-text exception).
- In tests: see `portal/tests/unit/static/css/banners/menu-drawer-contrast-allowlist.unit.test.mjs` and `menu-drawer-ink-contract.unit.test.mjs`.
